WEBVTT

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:06.100
Well, after a whole lot of stumbling and fussing about,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.400
everyone seems to have figured out why they fight,

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.060
but I'm not clear on this actually.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:13.820
Well, whatever.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.830
Dear Nergal, why are we getting stuck with even more hot shots?

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.140
Akito!

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.560
What's wrong? Does your tummy hurt?

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.050
Shut up.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:04.820
Were you in a fight?

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:06.600
Shut up! Go away!

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.360
Hey, want to learn a magic trick that'll turn Akito back to normal?

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.570
Close your eyes.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.970
Gross! What did you do that for?!

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.470
Goody, Akito's back to normal!

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:34.990
You...

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.970
Hey, wait, Yurika!

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:46.520
Not again.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.930
It happened over ten years ago.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:52.160
The Miracle Operation of the "Kiss?"
It happened over ten years ago.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.360
The Miracle Operation of the "Kiss?"

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.280
Are you still here?

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.450
The Admiral will be up at any moment.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.320
I'm going to pass. I'm not comfortable around him.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.930
Are you still suspicious about his involvement in Yamada's death?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:12.400
One of the Admiral's subordinates confessed to the crime and he was court-martialed!

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.230
I know.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:18.290
If you don't show up, the Captain will wonder about you.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.720
What is that supposed to mean?!

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.140
Oh nothing. Later.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.430
Now then...

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.700
Pardon the suddenness, but we've got orders.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:26.550
Admiral!

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.230
Yes?

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:30.020
While Nergal may have signed an alliance with the armed forces,

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.520
we have the right to refuse orders that we deem unacceptable.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:34.940
Yes, technically, you do.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.860
Understand that as captain, l, Misumaru Yurika,
will reject orders

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:42.370
that run afoul of the collective interests of this vessel's crew.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.310
You're saying you won't accept being treated like a pawn in a war.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:51.890
Well, you need not worry, because this mission isn't about fighting.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.510
Our goal is to elude enemy detection and rescue someone!

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.300
A rescue operation?

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.470
Although not on Mars, we remain under attack by Jovian forces,

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.970
and we must continue Nadesico's mission of saving innocent lives.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.810
Wouldn't you agree?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:15.480
As you can see, there are 2,637 Chulips on Earth.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.100
And here in the Arctic Ocean, we have Uchatsurawatosk Island.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.070
Our job is to rescue a goodwill ambassador from a certain nation

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.570
left behind on this island.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.250
Question...

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:26.700
Yes?

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.620
Why was the person left behind in a place like that?

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.510
The ambassador is a very enthusiastic researcher.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:36.700
While he was checking weather data, touring fisheries and such,

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.300
the Battas suddenly attacked, oh my!

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.750
Blizzard conditions persist nearly every day in the seas

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.230
around Uchatsurawatosk Island during this time of the year,

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:46.640
so it's not an easy place to get to.

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:52.810
Oh boy, this'll never work.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.150
Looks like the childhood friendship won't last much longer.

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.860
But his relationship with his new lover isn't going anywhere.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.650
Now's your chance!

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.070
Enough with the chit-chat about love!

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:07.490
In any case, the only ship that can pull this off is the Nadesico!

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:09.270
Understood, Captain?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.910
Yes! Let's do it!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:18.410
So the Nadesico headed off toward Uchatsurawatosk Island.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.340
But we pilots sure don't have anything to do.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.760
Guess we're supposed to save our strength for later.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:27.390
Savoring sweetness while saving strength.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:32.560
You don't look very disciplined.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.110
Come with me for a while.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.720
And it's not for the reason you people are thinking.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.410
I have something I've been meaning to ask you about.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:47.820
Ask me what?

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.740
It's about the Captain, I mean Yurika.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:51.660
Yurika?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.870
Are you going steady with her?

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:55.930
Why are you...

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:58.710
Why are you asking this all of a sudden?!

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.500
This is what she said.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:03.580
Well, I already have this person I have my heart set on!

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:07.140
The Prince Charming I've been dreaming of since I was a child!

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.720
I didn't agree to that!

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.230
I see, so you're not interested.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.100
Well, that works well for me.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.830
I'll take care of

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.780
Misumaru Yurika!

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.450
Hey, I don't remember clubbing being acceptable!

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.060
In real combat, it's no holds barred!

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.980
All right! Another round with close up combat allowed this time!

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:36.990
Sounds fine!

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.660
Ready... Go!

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.740
All right, eat this!

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:44.940
You still have a lot to learn.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.380
Oh yeah? How's this?!

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.800
We are entering the Bering Strait.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.800
The blizzard has reduced our visibility to zero.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.080
On the other hand, conditions for the enemy are also horrible.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:55.980
That is not necessarily a bad thing.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:59.670
Optical scanning indicates few reefs that pose any danger.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.750
It looks like we'll be able to make it through from the front.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.110
Engines at minimum power!

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:10.450
Oh, Nanako-san, your skin is smooth as a Hakata doll's!

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.920
Oh dear, Johnny!

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.950
How dare he touch a maiden's skin!

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.120
What a show off.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:19.270
You're worried about Nanako, aren't you?

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:20.390
Shut up!

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:21.500
What do brats know?!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.400
Akito-san...

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:24.710
Could you come with me?

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.800
Okay, here we are!

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.850
Is it all right for you not to be at your post?

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.370
They said the blizzard is so bad that the radio is useless.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.730
I don't have much to do now.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:36.950
Oh, I see.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.290
You don't either, right?

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:42.290
I heard that Izumi-san could easily handle this mission alone.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.150
Well yeah, as long as no opposing forces appear.

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:50.230
How about a early 21st century high school as the backdrop?

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:53.330
Let's leave the clothing at their default settings.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.110
I'll explain!

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:02.890
This room was created to relieve the crew's stress while in space.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:07.470
The system analyzes each person's brain waves,
conducts psychological analysis...

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:10.770
Okay, Akito-san! Time to enjoy school life just between the two of us.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.370
Let's go!

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:21.510
Akito-senpai!

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:25.090
What do you think?

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:26.070
How do I look?

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.860
Megumi-chan, that outfit...

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:32.240
Wow, look at how short the skirts were back in those days!

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.660
Oh, is this the first time you've been in here?

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:35.700
Uh, yeah...

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:40.370
In here, Akito-san is my mentor in an after-school club!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.500
Oh, come on! Relax! Relax!

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:48.130
How are we going to relieve any stress if you get all tensed up?

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.130
How am I not supposed to get tense?!

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.560
Come on! What's wrong, my Akito-senpai?!

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.230
Nothing. Not a thing.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:04.240
I'm glad I tweaked the setting for this to be a little more adult.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:10.190
Brake Time

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.960
Where did Megumi-san go?

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.510
Oh, are you interested in knowing, Ruri-ruri?

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:16.380
Yes.

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:17.870
She should be!

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.200
Should be in the virtual reality room with Akito-kun!

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:25.780
All alone, immersed in their world of amour.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:26.850
I like that.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.630
Are they on a date?

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:30.710
Wrapped up in love!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.590
Captain! Captain Misumaru!

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.980
What are you doing spacing out like that?

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.830
You should know better while we're on a mission!

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:40.560
Acting like that is why your boyfriend ran out on you!

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:47.510
Why is Erina-san, who's just a helmswoman, acting so bossy?

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:50.880
Well, she used to be secretary to the chairman of Nergal.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:51.520
She's stuck-up and thinks...

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.300
Everyone, please return to your seats!

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:53.900
Yes, Ma'am!

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:56.340
You two go down below to be on standby!

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:56.950
Yes, Ma'am.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.850
Do you understand, Captain?! Straighten up! Straighten up!

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:04.640
Akito, is it true? Do you really like Megu-chan more?

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.170
Why did you lock the door?

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.080
You wanted to talk to me about something. What is it?

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.840
Akito-senpai, there's something I'd like you to do for me.

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:15.010
What's that?

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.680
It's about the upcoming art competition.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:21.010
Please use me as your model!

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.740
I get it. So that's how this goes.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.940
Well, I don't know what to say!

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.120
I'm willing.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.220
For you...

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:41.870
No, you can't, Megumi-chan!

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.570
After all, we're...

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.830
still high school students!

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.750
No obstacles ahead, all clear.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.630
Switching to auto pilot.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.760
Captain! Captain!

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:58.810
Everyone's gone to lunch. What about you, Captain?

00:10:58.810 --> 00:10:59.980
Oh, I'm fine.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.630
Why don't you go ahead, Ruri-chan.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:02.070
Thank you.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:07.960
Brake Time

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.000
I love Akito!
Brake Time

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:10.060
Brake Time

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:13.570
Akito, how do you feel?

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:14.730
No!

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:16.780
You're a coward, senpai!

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.490
You took my first kiss from me.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.240
That's different from this.

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:23.160
Here, at least put this on!

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.990
Senpai, do you despise me?

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.900
Well...

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:32.510
I... I love you very much, senpai!

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:33.280
That's why...

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:35.120
Megumi-chan...

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:37.360
If those two...

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.390
If Akito is still together with Megumi-san...

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:43.730
No, I won't have it!

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:56.870
Senpai...

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.530
Megumi-chan...

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:02.450
Kiss me, Akito. That will carry me through!

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:03.240
Yurika?

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.370
Emergency

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.780
An emergency?!

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:12.860
Has the enemy detected us?

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:18.630
Maintain our shields and retreat!

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:20.680
Distortion Field holding steady.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.430
Ten seconds until we are out of their range.

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:25.190
Graviton sensors indicate numerous mobile enemy units.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.560
How far are we going to pull back?

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:29.100
We're considering the matter. For the moment hold present speed!

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:30.950
All Aestivalis pilots, prepare for launch...

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:52.080
Magnetic resonance results show the enemy's number and position.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:53.890
I just can't believe it!

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:57.020
Why did you go out of your way to draw the enemy's attention?!

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.310
No use crying over spilled milk.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:00.530
Why I ought to...

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:02.440
You have to keep looking ahead in life, right?

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:07.140
If someone is held responsible,
it should be me for leaving my post.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.060
System program administration is my responsibility.

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:10.240
I apologize.

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:15.370
Could Ruri-ruri be covering for the Captain?!

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:17.070
Has she graduated from calling people "BAKA-bakka"?

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:17.730
Baka.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:22.670
Since we were detected in the western passage,

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.700
we'll have to sneak through the eastern island straits.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:28.570
Flying at low altitude, our chances for running aground are 72%.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.870
These certainly aren't very good odds.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:31.160
Resting

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.820
The Nadesico will embark in ten minutes,

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:33.070
Resting

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:34.970
and we'll proceed through the eastern passage.

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:35.280
Resting

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.520
Aestivalis units are to stand by at alert status.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:38.090
That is all

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:38.540
Resting

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.330
I wonder what happened to the Captain?

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:43.370
She might be alone in a corner crying.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:45.550
I'll be right back!

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.680
Hey, Tenkawa!

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:48.600
Damn...

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:54.750
Yurika...

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:01.320
Akito!

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:02.240
Yurika...

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:23.110
This might sound strange coming from me,
but I have to say,

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:27.090
you're not at all yourself when you're depressed like this.

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.380
Akito-senpai...

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:32.720
Senpai!

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:37.660
I'm such a klutz,
and I keep messing things up for everyone!

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:44.270
You can't stand a dorky, slow, clumsy girl like me, can you?

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:49.950
Well, I...

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:51.660
I... I...

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.830
It would keep me going just a little longer.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:03.250
Well...

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:05.720
This magic will get you going again!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:07.410
Yurika...

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:14.220
Wait.

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.180
Say Akito, are you feeling sorry for me?

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:18.640
Sorry?

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.590
On Mars, I said if you kissed me,
I could handle it longer.

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:25.940
But you didn't kiss me because you wanted me to be tougher.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:30.720
This is just like back then. I see now how you felt then.

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.420
Akito isn't someone I can hide behind.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:34.830
Kiss me when you're in love with me.

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:37.290
Yurika-san?

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:39.710
Because...

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:43.710
Because that will be my first kiss!

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:46.760
Wait a minute!

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:48.280
Are you serious?

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.970
Yes, I'm serious!

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:51.460
That's not what I'm asking!

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.880
Enemy Attack

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:55.940
Oh, an enemy attack!

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:59.310
Let's go, Akito. Aren't pilots supposed to be on alert status?

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.620
Right...

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:08.910
Oh, so you decided to come back.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:10.670
I'm sorry for being late.

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:11.780
Status report, please!

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:14.200
We are currently proceeding through the reefs.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:17.500
This is no time to get bogged down!

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.620
Hurry up so that our goodwill ambassador doesn't starve!

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.290
Well that's easy for you to say.

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:24.960
But wouldn't the person freeze to death first when the fuel runs out?

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:27.280
Oh, well, that's not very likely.

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.320
Just hurry it up!

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:36.180
Yurika, give me the coordinates for the ambassador's location.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:37.100
Akito-san...

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:38.060
Yurika!

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.020
Reference the coordinates in Map A-13.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.400
Other Aestivalis, lay cover fire to assist Akito and the Nadesico!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:44.270
Roger!

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:52.720
I'd prefer you didn't grab all the good scenes.

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:54.270
Well, if you're interested in the Captain,

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:55.770
you should be more than willing to safeguard the Nadesico!

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:08.160
Ready? Formation Buttercup!

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:27.150
Where is the ambassador?

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:35.280
Damn it! I barely have enough energy without this!

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:39.370
Should've known, damn it!

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:50.510
No good! The visibility is so bad I can't hit him.

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:52.670
I know! I'll use this!

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:56.550
Eat this!

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:08.440
Gekigan Flare!

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:16.610
That can't be...

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:19.080
Akito...

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:22.040
He'll be back, I'm sure of it.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:25.210
Where is Tenkawa-kun?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:27.000
He's taking his sweet time.

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:28.250
He'll be back.

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:31.000
I see.

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:33.170
Ryoko...

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:34.510
Don't let yourself get down.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:35.160
Fool...

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:38.060
Don't you dare make a girl cry, Akito.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:41.780
This is getting hopeless, isn't it?

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:46.020
Even at max energy, he should be able to fly another 15 seconds.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:49.730
Electromagnetic static has lifted. Radio traffic is possible.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.990
Aestivalis identification signal cannot be detected.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.530
No transmissions either.

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:02.450
Akito...

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:05.620
Oh, our poor goodwill ambassador!

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:13.120
No, it's my fault!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.820
Because I screwed up!

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.010
Hey, Yurika!

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:20.010
Akito!

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:21.800
Could you come down and get me?

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.200
Where are you?

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.150
Just below you.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:31.900
Oh, Akito!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.820
Tenkawa, reporting back to base!

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:39.460
But Admiral, is this the goodwill ambassador you told us about?

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:44.640
Um, well, you see...

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.760
The military spent a whole lot of money on this lab bear

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:53.110
and experimental equipment, so we needed to rescue the bear.

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.910
But who'd risk their lives for a bear?

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:02.630
Thank goodness, Akito-san!

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.070
I was so worried about you!

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:06.060
You see, I was really, really...

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.240
I'm sorry, but I need to report to the Captain first.

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:25.160
Reporting back to base, Captain!

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:26.570
Well done.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:29.490
But most importantly, thank you, Akito.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.040
Has she really forgotten?

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:36.090
Nothing!

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:50.290
Our hit main theme, "You Get to Burning" plays on,

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:53.520
telling us to be ourselves, to be yourself, to be an individual!

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:56.570
As the age when men were men and women were women passes,

00:21:56.570 --> 00:21:58.240
the question is raised yet again.

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:00.750
What is the meaning of living like a man? Like a woman?!

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:02.660
The famous original author of "Saber Marionette J"

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:05.020
tackles this difficult question. His name is...

00:22:05.020 --> 00:22:06.540
Oh dear, no time left.

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:08.860
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:08.860 --> 00:22:10.520
"The Dangers of Femininity"

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:12.580
Let's watch it, everyone!
